  "lifecycle": {
   "scratchRoot": "host: mkdirat under the held operational-root fd, mode 0700, one per spawn; the host keeps the directory fd for the spawn lifetime; the path is delivered by the bootstrap successor member resultScratchRoot; SDK: opens it once at startup with O_DIRECTORY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC, checks uid and mode 0700, and holds that fd for every later openat",
   "he2Publish": "host writes <rid>.bin.tmp via openat(heldDir, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW), mode 0400, fsync, renameat to <rid>.bin, fsync directory, and only THEN sends effectResult (publish before result); the aggregate per-spawn accounting is charged before publication and a result that would exceed 64 MiB is FAILED without publication",
   "he1Stage": "SDK writes stage/<handle hex>.bin via openat(heldDir, O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC), fsync, close, records its own digest, then sends effectRequest; host openat(heldDir, stage/<handle hex>.bin, O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC), fstat admission (stage_file_admission), reads exactly size bytes once into a buffer allocated at that size, digests and commits FROM THE BUFFER by temp-then-rename into the staged class, unlinks the stage file (single-use handle), then RA/RCI/RCO and effectResult with the receipt rr:<rid>:<digest>:<length>; SDK compares the receipt digest to its own: RESULT.RECEIPT_MISMATCH is SDK-local",
   "he1Receipt": "the HE-1 rr:<rid>:<digest>:<length> is a RECEIPT ONLY: it authenticates the committed input bytes (digest and length of what the host committed from its buffer; rid is the host-minted commit id carried on the RCO record) and names NO file; the host publishes no receipt file for HE-1 and the SDK must not open one; writeHostState returns the receipt after comparing its digest with the bytes it staged",
   "cleanup": "result and stage files live until spawn end; the host removes the whole scratch root at spawn end; the SDK never deletes; a spawn that ends abnormally leaves nothing the next spawn can see (fresh directory name per spawn)"
  },
